1. Purpose
This policy establishes mandatory controls for the {{ control_family }} security domain at HYTech Solutions.
{% if status == 'deprecated' %}
NOTE: This policy has been superseded. Refer to the current active {{ control_family }} policy for enforcement requirements.
{% endif %}
The controls described herein are required to maintain the organisation's security posture and
comply with applicable regulatory frameworks.

2. Scope
This policy applies to all systems, personnel, and third-party integrations operating within
the HYTech Solutions environment that fall under the {{ control_family }} control domain.
Enforcement is the responsibility of the {{ enforcement_owner }}.

3. Control Requirements
The following controls are mandated under this policy:

| Control ID | Requirement | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
{% for ctrl in control_rows %}
| {{ ctrl.id }} | {{ ctrl.requirement }} | {{ ctrl.status }} |
{% endfor %}

All mandatory requirements must be implemented without exception unless a formal waiver has
been granted by the Chief Information Security Officer.

4. Risk Classification
This policy addresses {{ risk_level }} risk events in the {{ control_family }} domain.
Risk events in this category have the following characteristics:
- Likelihood: {{ risk_likelihood }}
- Potential impact: {{ risk_impact }}
- Detection difficulty: {{ detection_difficulty }}

5. Incident Response and Escalation
In the event of a policy violation or security incident, the following escalation timeline applies:

| Risk Level | Escalation Deadline | Primary Contact | Secondary Contact |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Critical | 1 hour | {{ enforcement_owner }} | Chief Information Security Officer |
| High | 4 hours | {{ enforcement_owner }} | Security Operations Lead |
| Medium | 24 hours | {{ enforcement_owner }} | Security Operations Lead |
| Low | 3 business days | {{ enforcement_owner }} | Security Operations Lead |

All incidents must be logged in the Security Incident Tracking System within the above deadlines.

6. Mandatory Requirements
The following actions are required for compliance with control(s) {{ control_ids | join(', ') }}:
{% for req in mandatory_requirements %}
- {{ req }}
{% endfor %}

7. Prohibited Actions
The following actions are explicitly prohibited under this policy:
{% for item in prohibited_actions %}
- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}

8. Exceptions
{% if exception_allowed %}
Exceptions to this policy may be approved by the Chief Information Security Officer under the
following conditions:
- A documented business justification is provided
- Compensating controls are identified and implemented
- The exception is time-limited (maximum {{ max_exception_days }} days)
- The exception is reviewed at each {{ review_frequency_days }}-day review cycle
{% else %}
No exceptions are permitted for {{ risk_level }} risk controls in the {{ control_family }} domain.
All requirements in Section 6 are non-negotiable.
{% endif %}

9. Audit and Compliance
The Security Operations team conducts reviews of this policy's compliance every {{ review_frequency_days }} days.
Non-compliance identified during audit must be remediated within {{ remediation_days }} business days.
Evidence of compliance must be documented and available for audit at all times.

